\subtree{
  \title{Work order without circular gates}
  \ol{
    \li{Inventory, universe and seal prototypes; small discrete category/groupoid examples.}
    \li{Augmented algebra/shapes and their required diagram-model lemmas (\ref{at-fd-0007}).}
    \li{Reduced gluing/replacement and the standalone categorical framing (core parts of \ref{at-fd-0003}/4), plus monodromy and the discrete equivalence tests.}
    \li{State/prove the remaining equivalence laws; build relative walking constructions and the nondiscrete example (\ref{at-fd-0005}/8).}
    \li{Check that example's categorical extraction to finish \ref{at-fd-0004}; finish the scoped pasting, symmetry, and final audit gates.}
  }
  \p{The subparts of \ref{at-fd-0004} are deliberately separated: its framing is a prerequisite of the example, while its final root comparison is a client of that example. A gate-level mutual reference does not authorize a circular Lean proof.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Interpreting failures}
  \p{Universe offsets, object reduction, and specification packaging have direct candidate repairs. The old unconditional \code{hP} is removed from required architecture, so failure to recover it is not failure of \ref{ms-foundation}. The material research risks are the augmented arity/model theory, coherent \code{Mod}, and the intended equivalence/categorical comparison. A negative result for those could require a different root presentation or a smaller first release. It would not by itself refute the broader goal of a common, interface-driven categorical library.}
}
